.TH M3U8-DOWNLOADER 1 "July 2026" "m3u8-downloader 4.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
m3u8-downloader \- download, filter, and merge m3u8 streams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B m3u8-downloader
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ url ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B m3u8-downloader
opens the terminal UI when run without a URL. When a URL is provided, it
downloads an m3u8 playlist, optionally filters advertising segments by keyword
or regular expression, downloads media segments concurrently, and merges them
into an MP4 file with FFmpeg.
.PP
The command supports media playlists directly and master playlists with multiple
variants. By default, the highest bandwidth variant is selected unless a variant
index is specified.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I url
Optional m3u8 playlist URL to download directly. This can be a media playlist or
a master playlist. If omitted, the terminal UI is opened.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \--help
Show command help and exit.
.TP
.BI \-o " OUTPUT"
.TQ
.BI \--output " OUTPUT"
Write the merged MP4 file to
.IR OUTPUT .
.TP
.BI \--work-dir " WORK_DIR"
Directory used for downloaded TS segments. The directory is created if needed.
.TP
.BI \--header " HEADER"
Add an HTTP request header. Use the form
.IR "Name: value" .
This option can be repeated. A common use is passing a Referer header.
.TP
.BI \--keyword " KEYWORD"
Filter out segments whose URL or title contains
.IR KEYWORD .
This option can be repeated.
.TP
.B \--regex
Treat filter keywords as regular expressions instead of plain text.
.TP
.BI \--threads " THREADS"
Number of concurrent segment download workers.
.TP
.BI \--variant " VARIANT"
Select a master playlist variant by zero-based index. If omitted, the highest
bandwidth variant is used.
.TP
.BI \--dump-filtered " DUMP_FILTERED"
Write the filtered m3u8 playlist to
.I DUMP_FILTERED
before downloading. This is useful for checking which segments remain after
filtering.
.TP
.B \--keep-segments
Keep downloaded TS segment files after the MP4 merge finishes.
.TP
.B \--tui
Open the terminal UI explicitly.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Open the terminal UI
.EX
m3u8-downloader
.EE
.SS Basic download
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://example.com/video/index.m3u8" -o video.mp4
.EE
.SS Use a Referer header
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://example.com/video.m3u8" \
  -o video.mp4 \
  --header "Referer: https://example.com/"
.EE
.SS Increase download concurrency
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://example.com/video.m3u8" -o video.mp4 --threads 16
.EE
.SS Filter ad segments by keywords
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://example.com/video.m3u8" \
  -o video.mp4 \
  --keyword /video/adjump/
.EE
.SS Filter with regular expressions and inspect the playlist
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://example.com/video.m3u8" \
  -o video.mp4 \
  --keyword "adjump|banner|promo" \
  --regex \
  --dump-filtered filtered.m3u8
.EE
.SS Select a master playlist variant
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://example.com/master.m3u8" -o video.mp4 --variant 0
.EE
.SS Keep downloaded segment files
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://example.com/video.m3u8" \
  -o video.mp4 \
  --work-dir ./segments \
  --keep-segments
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/m3u8-downloader/config.json
Desktop application configuration file.
.TP
.I /usr/share/m3u8-downloader/
Installed application source and shared files in the Debian package.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
The Debian package depends on Python 3, requests, aiohttp, PyQt6, Textual, and
FFmpeg. FFmpeg must be available for MP4 merging.
